# RetroArchiver - the window's texts in English
#
# UTF-8, one key=text per line; lines starting with # are comments.
# Blanks around the key and the text are dropped.
# Escapes in the texts: \n new line, \t tab, \s space (for a text that
# starts or ends with one), \\ backslash.
# A text with %ls, %d, %lu... is a format: a translation keeps the same
# conversions in the same order (%% for a percent sign), otherwise the
# window uses the English text. Arguments cannot be reordered: rephrase.
#
# A new language: copy this file to lang\<code>.lng, with the ISO 639
# code of the language (de.lng, fr.lng...), and translate the texts.
# language.name is the name shown in the window's menu. Keys that are
# missing stay in English.

# the language itself
language.name=English
format.decimal=.
format.date=YYYY-MM-DD

