# automatic mode
auto.waiting=Automatic read: waiting for the disk in drive %ls
auto.count.one=Reading %ls in one second
auto.count.many=Reading %ls in %d seconds
auto.count.label=Label: %ls.\s
auto.count.text=Esc stops the countdown and waits for you to press Read (F5); Enter reads now, Alt+S skips the disk.
auto.ask.title=This looks like the same %ls as %ls: read it again?
auto.ask.text=It has the same serial number (%04lX-%04lX)%ls as %ls, already read. If it really is %ls press Read (F5); otherwise insert the right %ls and it starts by itself, or Skip (Alt+S).
auto.ask.samelabel=\sand the same label
auto.removed=Disk removed from drive %ls: insert the next one
auto.disc.removed=Disc removed from drive %ls: insert the next one
auto.slow=The drive answers slowly: a change is noticed only if you remove the disk and then insert it
auto.nodriver=Automatic read not available: fdrawcmd.sys does not answer on drive %ls. Press Read (F5) when the disk is in.
auto.stopped=Automatic read stopped for this disk: press Read (F5) when you are ready.
auto.typing=You are typing: the read starts when you press Enter or Read (F5).

# the volume label
label.reading=Reading the disk label...
label.kept=Disk label: %ls (the one you typed stays)
label.read=Label read from the disk: %ls
label.none=The disk has no volume label
label.nodisk=No disk in drive %ls
label.unknown=Windows does not recognise the disk: the label is taken from the image after the read

# the banners while waiting for a disk
insert.floppy=Insert %ls %d of %d
insert.floppy.manual=Then press Enter or Read (F5); F2 reads the label again, Alt+S skips the disk. Disk label (optional):
insert.floppy.auto=Automatic read: as soon as the disk is in the drive it starts by itself. Enter or F5 reads now, Alt+S skips, Esc goes back to reading by hand. Disk label (optional):
insert.floppy.auto.next=Automatic read: remove the disk just read and insert this one, it starts by itself. Enter or F5 reads now, Alt+S skips, Esc goes back to reading by hand. Disk label (optional):
insert.optical=Insert %ls %d of %d in drive %ls
insert.optical.one=Insert the %ls in drive %ls
insert.optical.manual=Close the drive, wait until its light stops blinking, then press Enter or Read (F5); F2 reads the label again, Alt+S skips. Reading with DiscImageCreator takes 10 to 30 minutes. Label of the %ls (optional):
insert.optical.auto=Automatic read: %ls, it starts by itself when Windows sees it (10 to 30 minutes). Enter or F5 reads now, Alt+S skips, Esc goes back to reading by hand. Label of the %ls (optional):
insert.optical.first=insert the disc
insert.optical.next=remove the disc just read and insert this one
unreadable.title=%ls %d of %d: reading %ls is not available yet
unreadable.text=The %ls stays to be read and the box stays open: resume it with Resume when RetroArchiver can read %ls. Press Skip to go on.
duplicate.title=%ls is identical to %ls
duplicate.other=another disk
duplicate.text.auto=Remove the %ls and insert the right %ls: it starts by itself. Or Read again (F5) or Skip (Alt+S). The wrong reads are in set-aside, not deleted; if the two disks really are the same, read it again: the second time it is kept.
duplicate.text=Remove the %ls, insert the right %ls and press Read again (F5), or Skip (Alt+S). The wrong reads are in set-aside, not deleted; if the two disks really are the same, read it again: the second time it is kept.
retry.interrupted=%ls %d: read interrupted
retry.failed=%ls %d: read failed
retry.text.interrupted=Press Retry to read it again, Skip to go to the next one, or close the window: the box stays open and you resume it from the archive
retry.text.floppy.auto=Check the disk and put it back in the drive: it starts by itself. Or press Retry (F5) or Skip (Alt+S).
retry.text.floppy=Check the disk, put it back in the drive and press Retry (F5), or Skip (Alt+S).
retry.text.why=%ls\nThen press Retry (F5), or Skip (Alt+S).
retry.text.disc=Check the disc (the right type, clean), put it back in the drive and press Retry (F5), or Skip (Alt+S).
retry.protection.title=%ls %d: read it again looking for copy protections
retry.protection.failed=The read was made without the copy protection scan: Retry (F5) reads it again with the scan (DiscImageCreator /sf), Skip (Alt+S) goes on.
retry.protection.errors=The read, made without the copy protection scan, has errors: a protection can cause them. Retry (F5) reads it again with the scan (DiscImageCreator /sf); Skip (Alt+S) keeps what was read.
retry.protection.off.title=%ls %d: read it again without looking for copy protections
retry.protection.off.text=With the copy protection scan (DiscImageCreator /sf) the drive reset itself (UNIT_ATTENTION, timeouts): the scan is the cause, not the disc. Retry (F5) reads it again without it, Skip (Alt+S) goes on.

# the banners during the read
start.title=Preparing the box...
start.text=Creating the package or resuming the open one.
work.floppy.text=%ls %d of %d%ls. Do not remove the disk until the read is finished.
work.reread=The reads do not match: one more read
work.fragile=Fragile disk: a single careful read
work.reading=Reading: do not remove the disk
work.optical.text=%ls %d of %d in drive %ls%ls. Do not open the drive until the read is finished: a whole CD takes 10 to 30 minutes.
work.optical.reread=One read is not enough: reading the %ls again to compare
work.optical.reading=Reading: do not remove the %ls
answer.skip=Skipping %ls.
answer.later=%ls stays to be read.
answer.closing=Closing the box...
answer.closing.text=Computing the SHA-256 hashes of the files and checking them again.
stop.title=Stopping the read...
stop.dic=DiscImageCreator stops in a moment. The half-finished read does not stay in the package.
stop.samdisk=SAMdisk stops in a moment.
stop.compare=The comparison finishes by itself in a moment
stop.compare.last=This is the last disk of the box: wait here for the outcome, there is no next disk to ask for
stop.compare.next=When it asks for the next disk you can close the window: the box stays open and you resume it from the archive
stop.none=There is no read to stop here
stop.none.text=Wait a few seconds.

# the log
log.box.done=Box %ls: package closed and verified.
log.box.complete=complete
log.box.incomplete=incomplete
log.error=ERROR: %ls
log.noleadin=Drive %ls cannot read the lead-in or the lead-out: saved in RetroArchiver.ini ([Optical] NoLeadInDrives). From now on its data CDs are read with DiscImageCreator data straight away; audio and mixed CDs need another drive.
banner.error=Error

# the end of the box
end.complete=Box complete: %ls of %d
end.incomplete=Box closed incomplete: %ls of %d
end.closed.text=%ls.\nThe package is closed and verified.%ls
end.aside=\sThe reads set aside stay outside the data: look at them and, if they are not needed, delete them.
end.later=\nResume it from the archive when RetroArchiver can read %ls.
end.later.both=CDs and DVDs
end.later.cd=CDs
end.later.dvd=DVDs
end.open=Box left open
end.open.how=\nTo resume it: Archive, then double-click the box.
end.failed=Archiving failed
end.failed.text=%ls%lsRead the log below, fix the problem and try again with New box.
summary.nothing=no media

# questions and errors
finish.ask.one=Still missing: %ls.\n\nIf the box is closed now it will be incomplete, with that medium missing, and it can no longer be resumed from the archive.\n\nClose the box?
finish.ask.many=Still missing: %ls.\n\nIf the box is closed now it will be incomplete, with those media missing, and it can no longer be resumed from the archive.\n\nClose the box?
close.ask=A box is in progress. Leave it open (it can be resumed from the archive) and close?
error.memory=Not enough memory.
error.nostart=Cannot start the session.

